      "writtenOn": "2026-06-23T20:21:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Both are necessary:\nBarrier 1, acquire: Is necessary so that the subsequent load is not reordered prior to the barrier (which would cause it to read stale data before other threads finish writing).\nBarrier 1, release: Is necessary so that prior writes to shared memory are fully flushed and not reordered after the barrier.\nBarrier 2, acquire: Is necessary so that subsequent writes are not reordered prior to the barrier (which would cause other threads to overwrite the data before the load happens).\nBarrier 2, release: Is necessary so that the prior load completes and is not reordered after the barrier.\n\nAt a meta-level, we also want uniform behavior across the backends. (I.e. workgroupUniformLoad() can be used somewhat creatively if you can also assume that it\u0027s a normal barrier). Tint simply adds their the workgroupBarrier, which we could maybe do here for clarity?\nhttps://crsrc.org/c/third_party/angle/third_party/dawn/src/tint/lang/wgsl/reader/lower/lower.cc;drc\u003dd372be1054684effe1d593ce4f8255fe05e27a65;l\u003d233",
      "parentUuid": "6040abfc_28e10f98",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2592,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2593,
